  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 245 PM MST MON NOV 9 2026\nAn upper level ridge will remain over the area on Thursday with\nstrong southwest flow aloft with multiple low pressure systems \noffshore in the Gulf of Alaska. This will keep temperatures well\nabove normal through Friday. Temperatures will be near record \nhighs Thursday and Friday with breezy to windy conditions. A \ncold front will approach the area on Friday. Gusts 35-50 mph are\npossible on Friday across the open terrain of southeast Oregon \nwith gusts 20-40 mph elsewhere. Still high uncertainty on the \ntiming of the cold front, with differences up to 12 to 24 hours,\nbut showers increase across the area late Friday night into \nSaturday. There is significant differences in the models \nSaturday and beyond, but conditions are favoring cooler and \nunsettled late in the weekend with mountain snows early next \nweek.",
